      "node_id": "kg_doc_1",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Eugene Paul \"E. P.\" Wigner (Hungarian: \"Wigner Jenő Pál\" ; November 17, 1902 – January 1, 1995), was a Hungarian-American theoretical physicist, engineer and mathematician. He received half of the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1963 \"for his contributions to the theory of the atomic nucleus and the elementary particles, particularly through the discovery and application of fundamental symmetry principles\".",
